source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: The `|` a backslash run stands in front of closes the row and stays in the cell: Jira renders one data cell holding `a`, a forced newline and a literal `|`, and reads `b|` as a paragraph below the table.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|a\\|
b|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />|</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>

<p>b|</p>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||
|a\\|
:::

b|
-- warnings.json --
[]
